<!--meta {"lead": "HairPop sounds like a knowledgeable friend who books braiders: warm, specific and honest about what is confirmed and what is not.", "description": "Voice, sentence case, button verbs, numbers, dates, times and prices, request vs appointment vocabulary, message formulas and a microcopy library.", "covers": "Voice, sentence case, button verbs, dates/times/prices, request vs appointment, error and empty formulas, microcopy library"} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>Customers choose someone to spend five hours with their hair. Copy builds that confidence by being <b>specific</b> (Nia, Sat 24 Oct, $180–$240), <b>honest</b> (an estimate is an estimate; a request is not an appointment), and <b>calm</b> (failures say what is safe before what went wrong). The <a href="../foundations/content.html">content foundation</a> has the full style rules; this pattern shows how they combine on screens.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Warm, not cute.</b> "Find a style that feels like you." Not "Slay your next look!!"</li>
    <li><b>Specific, not generic.</b> "Nia will reply with the final time and price." Not "We’ll be in touch."</li>
    <li><b>Honest about status.</b> "Awaiting Nia’s reply", never "Booked" before she accepts.</li>
    <li><b>Second person for Maya, first names for braiders.</b></li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="when"><h2><a href="#when">When to use which</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Moment</th><th scope="col">Tone</th><th scope="col">Example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Discovery (gallery, style detail)</td><td>Inviting, sensory</td><td>"Gentle at the root · 4–7 hours · typically $160–$300"</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Choosing a braider</td><td>Factual, comparable</td><td>"4.9 ★ from 86 reviews · Toronto West · knotless braids from $180"</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Requesting and waiting</td><td>Clear about what happens next</td><td>"This is a request, not a confirmed appointment."</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Something went wrong</td><td>Calm, reassuring first</td><td>"Your details are safe. Check your connection and try again."</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Legal, privacy, cookies</td><td>Plain, short sentences</td><td>"Choose whether optional usage data may be stored."</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <h3>Request or appointment?</h3>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Status</th><th scope="col">Say</th><th scope="col">Never say</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Sent, waiting for the braider</td><td>request, "Awaiting reply", "estimated price"</td><td>booking, appointment, confirmed, "your price"</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Braider accepted</td><td>appointment, "Confirmed", "confirmed estimate: $210"</td><td>request</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Visit happened</td><td>"Completed", "your visit with Nia on Sat 3 Oct"</td><td>"past booking"</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Withdrawn by Maya</td><td>"Cancelled", "request cancelled"</td><td>"deleted"</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="structure"><h2><a href="#structure">Structure</a></h2>
  <p>One screen, every content rule: eyebrow, a title that speaks to Maya, a subtitle of facts, an honest status, a next step named with a verb.</p>
  <div class="ds-frame"><div class="ds-frame__body">
    <div class="page-header"><div><p class="eyebrow">Appointments</p><p style="font: var(--text-h1); letter-spacing: var(--letter-spacing-tight);">Your appointment with Nia</p><p class="subtitle">Request HP-1048 · Sat 24 Oct at 10:00 am · awaiting Nia’s reply.</p></div></div>
    <section class="card stack" aria-label="Request HP-1048">
      <span class="badge badge--warning">Awaiting reply</span>
      <h2>Medium knotless braids</h2>
      <p><strong>Sat 24 Oct · 10:00 am</strong> with Nia Okafor</p>
      <p>Estimated price: $180–$240. Nia will confirm the final price.</p>
      <p>Location shared after Nia accepts.</p>
      <div class="cluster"><a class="btn" href="../../mocks/dialogs/change-appointment/default.html">Request a change</a><a class="btn btn--link" href="../../mocks/dialogs/cancel-appointment/default.html">Cancel request</a></div>
    </section>
  </div></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  <h3>Message formulas</h3>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Message</th><th scope="col">Formula</th><th scope="col">Example</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Field error</td><td>What to do + example or limit</td><td>"Enter an email address like name@example.com."</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Load error</td><td>We couldn’t [verb] [thing] + what is safe + what to try</td><td>"We couldn’t load your appointments. Your details are safe. Try again."</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Action failed</td><td>[Thing] not [done] + what is kept + retry</td><td>"Review not posted. Your words are saved. Please try again."</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Empty</td><td>No [things] yet + when they appear + action</td><td>"No appointments yet. When you request a visit, you’ll find it here."</td></tr>
      <tr><td>No results</td><td>No [things] match + the one change most likely to help</td><td>"No braiders match these filters. Try a wider price range."</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Success</td><td>Outcome + what happens next</td><td>"Request sent to Nia. She will reply with the final time and price."</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Confirmation</td><td>Question with object + consequence</td><td>"Cancel request HP-1048? Nia will see that you no longer need this time."</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <h3>Numbers, dates, times and prices</h3>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Thing</th><th scope="col">Write</th><th scope="col">Not</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Date</td><td>Sat 24 Oct (add the year only outside the current one)</td><td>10/24/2026, October 24th</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Time</td><td>10:00 am, 9:42 am</td><td>10AM, 10:00</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Date and time</td><td>Sat 24 Oct · 10:00 am, or "Sat 24 Oct at 10:00 am" in a sentence</td><td>24 Oct, 10am</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Price range</td><td>$180–$240 (en dash, no spaces, both dollar signs)</td><td>$180-240, $180 - $240</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Durations</td><td>4–7 hours, about 5 hours</td><td>4-7hrs</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Ratings and counts</td><td>4.9 ★ · 86 reviews; 1,284 reviews</td><td>4.90/5 (86)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>References</td><td>HP-1048</td><td>#1048, hp1048</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Punctuation</td><td>Curly apostrophes and quotes (you’re, Nia’s), the ellipsis character (…)</td><td>you're, ...</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Write once for 360px: titles of eight words or fewer, button labels of three or four words, subtitles that can wrap at a " · " separator.</li>
    <li>Never truncate a person’s name, a price or a date; let it wrap.</li>
    <li>Do not write different copy per breakpoint; shorten the source instead.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Link and button text make sense alone: "View Nia’s profile", "Cancel request" (2.4.4).</li>
    <li>Icon-only controls get a verb-and-object label: "Close dialog", "Dismiss: Time confirmed" (a toast's dismiss names its title).</li>
    <li>A visible label is part of the accessible name (2.5.3): the link that reads "Updates 2" is named "Updates 2, 2 unread".</li>
    <li>Status words appear as text, not colour alone: "Awaiting reply" on the badge.</li>
    <li>Plain language: short sentences, common words, no idioms that do not translate.</li>
    <li>Decorative glyphs (★, →, ·) are carried by the surrounding text or <code>aria-hidden</code>; a rating on its own reads "4.9 out of 5 stars" through visually hidden text.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <h3>Microcopy library</h3>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Context</th><th scope="col">Use</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Primary actions</td><td>Send request · Request with Nia · See braiders for this style · Post review · Save changes · Sign in · Create account · Send reset link · Save password · Resend email</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Secondary actions</td><td>Find braiders · Filters · Request a change · View request · View appointment · Explore styles</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Safe actions in dialogs</td><td>Keep request · Keep current time · Keep browsing · Stay signed in</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Destructive</td><td>Cancel request · Sign out · Send report</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Recovery</td><td>Try again · Retry reviews · Clear filters</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Statuses</td><td>Awaiting reply · Confirmed · Completed · Cancelled · Unread · Read</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Optional field</td><td>(optional) after the label</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Loading</td><td>Sending your request to Nia… · Refreshing braiders near Toronto…</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Offline</td><td>You’re offline. Your details stay here. Connect before sending.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Footer</td><td>HairPop · Made for confident hair decisions · Terms · Privacy</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>Sentence case everywhere, including buttons, titles, tabs and badges (badges are uppercased by CSS but written in sentence case).</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><p>Estimated price: $180–$240. Nia will confirm the final price.</p></div><figcaption>An estimate is labelled as one, with who confirms it.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><p>Your appointment is booked for $180.</p></div><figcaption>Calling a pending request booked, with a single price.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><button class="btn btn--primary" type="button">Send request</button></div><figcaption>A verb phrase that says what happens.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><button class="btn btn--primary" type="button">Submit</button><button class="btn" type="button">OK</button></div><figcaption>Generic labels that could mean anything.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

